<title>USA: WesterFed says shareholders okay merger.</title>
<headline>WesterFed says shareholders okay merger.</headline>
<dateline>MISSOULA, Mont. 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>WesterFed Financial Corp and Security Bancorp said on Tuesday their shareholders had approved the merger of the two companies.</p>
<p>WesterFed Financial is the holding company for Western Federal Savings Bank, an operater of 19 offices in Montana.</p>
<p>As of December 31, 1996, WesterFed Financial had total assets of $563.6 million, total deposits of $343.8 million and stockholders' equity of $79.5 million.</p>
<p>Montana-based Security Bancorp, parent of Security Bank FSB, had total assets of $377.8 million, deposits of $290.7 million and stockholders' equity of $33.0 million at Dec. 31.</p>
